1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of John Tiitto / Teto and Elizabeth Lungi. Husband to Theadora Ahola-Olson. He emigrated to the USA in 1879 and settled in Calumet, Houghton County, Michigan. He and his wife Dora were married on November 17, 1
2 CONC 898. The family moved to Peterborough, NH about 1905 before settling in Fitchburg, MA around 1907. Matthew worked as a printer for the Finnish newspaper "Raivaaja" in Fitchburg. His father and some of his brothers were also instru
2 CONC mental in the operation of the news publication. Matthew and Dora were the parents of 11 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lillian Florence Teto 1899/1975 Violet Marion (Teto) Day / 1902/1923 Gladys Annie Teto 1903/ Hattie Gwendolyn (Teto) Mercier 1904/1997 Mildred Adeline Teto 1906/1906 (4 months) Mildred Lucille (Teto) Malcolm Richard 1907/1938 Matt
2 CONC hew Howard Teto 1909/1909 (3 months) Hazel Adeline (Teto) Cormier O'Connor 1913/1978 Dorothy Edith Elizabeth (Teto) Sullivan 1915/1991 (Stillborn) Teto 1917/1917 Ruth Violet (Teto) Wood 1926/1998
2 CONT --------------------
