1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Violet was the second child of Matthew and Dora (Olson) Teto, born in Calumet, Houghton County, Michigan on March 27, 1902. She graduated from Fitchburg (MA) high school on June 19, 1919. In November 1922 at the ag
2 CONC e of 20, she married Loren Jesse Day and they lived in New York city. On March 4, 1923, she passed away at 10:50 PM in Roosevelt Hospital in Manhattan, NY. An autopsy was performed and the report submitted to the New York Departme
2 CONC nt of Health stated that she had died from the following causes. The chief cause of death, (determined by the autopsy), was acute and chronic endocarditis of the mitral and aortic valves, with acute suppurative endometritis, possi
2 CONC bly caused by an abortion.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body was subsequently transported back to her home town of Fitchburg, Worcester County, Massachusetts and she was buried on March 7, 1923 in Forest Hill Cemetery.
