1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gladys's first child:.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wallace Teto Sr. was born in Fitchburg, Worcester County, Massachusetts in 1923, the son of Gladys Annie Teto and an unknown father. Subsequent Y-DNA testing has uncovered the high possibility that his birth father was Harry Don 
2 CONC Kanfer (1885-1942). After his birth he was raised by his grandparents, Matthew Teto and Dora (Olson) Teto before marrying Ellen M (Taylor) Teto on October 12, 1946. He is survived by 3 children, 2 grandchildren, and 3 great-grandc
2 CONC hildren."
2 CONT
2 CONT Gladys Teto's second child.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Caroline Teto was the daughter of Gladys Annie Teto and George Branning. Her father was born in New Hampshire with that surname. It is unproven, but the possibility lies with the father being George Horton Brannen who was born in
2 CONC  Canada and living in Manchester, NH at the time. Mother Gladys Annie Teto had bounced around from Fitchburg, MA where she abandoned her first son in 1923, to Hartford, CT where she was arrested in December 1924 for prostitution. 
2 CONC Her next appearance is in Manchester, NH in 1930 where she is working in a shoe shop. Daughter Caroline died at the age of 2 months and 9 days from complications of an enlarged liver, jaundice, and eresypelatus. She was buried in 
2 CONC the public ground area of Pine Grove Cemetery in Manchester, Hillsborough County, New Hampshire and her remains lie in grave #3386. Besides her mother and father, she also left a half-brother, who was the son of Gladys and an unkn
2 CONC own father. "
