2 CONT * Michigan,1940 federal census, Population schedules: Houghton County, Chassell township: https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89M1-J9DW?i=21&personaUrl=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%3A1%3AK4LH-4PV
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110306844/alice-margaret-kivari
2 CONT
2 CONT "CHASSELL - Alice M. Kivari, 91, a former resident of Chassell, passed away Thursday morning, May 2, 2013, at the Delaware House of PortagePointe in Hancock where she had been a resident patient for the past four years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born Jan. 16, 1922, in the Snake River Hill area, a daughter of the late Thomas and Mary (Kurtti) Luusua. As a child, she attended the Snake River Hill School.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice then went to work on the family farm. She later moved to the Detroit area during World War II where she had worked in the airplane assembly plants to help the war effort.
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 19, 1949, she was united in marriage to Henry Kivari. The couple had resided in the Detroit area until 1982 when they moved to make their retirement home in Chassell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Kivari was a member of the Old Apostolic Lutheran Church in Hancock.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceding her in death were her husband, Henry on April 23, 2007; her infant daughter; her parents; brothers and sister, William, Mildred Peterson, Harold, Lawrence, Kenneth and Roy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her children, Warren (Tarja) Kivari of Chassell, Rachel (Daniel) Pedersen of South Haven, Minn., Norman (Carol) Kivari of Blain, Minn. and Andrew (Jana) Kivari of Holly, Mich.; 33 grandchildren; 46 great-grandchildre
2 CONC n; numerous nieces, nephews and cousins."
