2 CONT Veli Juho Järvelä Ellis Islandilla. "New York Passenger Arrival Lists (Ellis Island), 1892-1924", database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QGP3-P3MQ : 20 August 2019), Gustaf Kastama in entry for
2 CONC  Juho Jarvela, 1899.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirjassa New York Mills, 75 years: MR. AND. MRS. GUSTAV KASTAMA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustav Kastama was born in Finland, October 22,  1862. He was educated in the schools of Finland after  which he went to sea for two years. Coming to the  United States he enlisted in the U. S. Navy and served  for eight years. He
2 CONC  also became a citizen at that time.  In 1892 he went to work in the gold mines in the Black  Hills of South Dakota. Here, in 1897, he met and mar-  ried Miss Josephine Tuomela of Deer Creek township.  Mrs. Kastama was born in Fin
2 CONC land on April 20, 1872.  She came to this country with her parents, Mr. and  Mrs. Andrew Tuomela, in 1874. In 1895 she went to  South Dakota where she was employed until she mar-  ried Gustav Kastama in November 1897. After their 
2 CONC  marriage they returned to this community and moved  onto her parents' farm. They were the parents of seven  boys, three of whom have died. Remaining children are  Gustav, farming near Ponsford; Andrew, living on the  home farm, C
2 CONC aleb in Minneapolis and Henry in Minne-  apolis. They are both deceased.
