1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Caroline Teto was the daughter of Gladys Annie Teto and George Branning. I could find no father born in New Hampshire with that surname. It is unproven, but the possibility lies with the father being George Horton 
2 CONC Brannen who was born in Canada and living in Manchester, NH at the time. Mother Gladys Annie Teto had bounced around from Fitchburg, MA where she abandoned her first son in 1923, to Hartford, CT where she was arrested in December 
2 CONC 1924 for prostitution. Her next appearance is in Manchester, NH in 1930 where she is working in a shoe shop. Daughter Caroline died at the age of 2 months and 9 days from complications of an enlarged liver, jaundice, and eresypela
2 CONC tus. She was buried in the public ground area of Pine Grove Cemetery in Manchester, Hillsborough County, New Hampshire and her remains lie in grave #3386. Besides her mother and father, she also left a half-brother, who was the so
2 CONC n of Gladys and an unknown father.
