1 CONT
1 CONT May 10, said to have come back from Hailuoto.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1st one in area to have successful breast cancer surgery in 1940's.
1 CONT
1 CONT Glaucoma caused her to be blind before 1945.  Martha took care of her in her last days.
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried in Keweenaw Bay cemetery.
1 CONT
1 CONT About 1948-9 John and Kristina with Carl and Ida visited Oulu.  Arnold saw them and never realized that Kristina was Gustaf Johnson's sister.
1 CONT Arnold may have been told but did not "understand" who this woman was.  Ida stood by Kristina and said "Edwin's son is standing in front of you now" in Finnish.   She gave Arnold a silver dollar to remember her by.  That moment ha
1 CONC s never been forgotten.
