0 @N6000000001498704052@ NOTE
1 CONT Arrived in Baltimore, MD 19 December 1909 on the "Breslau" from Bremen, Germany. Family lore said he traveled here twice but was sent back for lack of funds. This was substantiated in 2001 with the discovery of his first passenger
1 CONC  ship record. He, in fact, came on the S.S. Bremen from Bremen arriving in N.Y. on 30 June 1909. He was labeled "LPC" (Likely to be a Public Charge) and deported after 12 days at Ellis Island when he lost his appeal.  Their marria
1 CONC ge was filled with separations and was not a happy one.
1 CONT
1 CONT His Social Security # 132-09-5912
1 CONT
1 CONT Birthdate is uncertain: Petition for Naturalization says 15 Feb 1885; Social Sec. Application says 15 Mar 1883; Death Certificate says 10 Mar 1884. World War I Draft Registration gives the 15 Feb 1885 date.
1 CONT Spent a lot of time at the painters’ union building at Pitkin and Stone (now Mother Gaston Blvd.)
1 CONT
1 CONT 1910 census says “Harry Confor,” and shows him as a packer in a clothing store, but this is the right person; address and head of household match information on sister Chulya’s passenger ship manifest.
